xceed the harms of decentralized deployment. If information processing were inherently extractive rather than generative, my argument for open access would collapse into a defense of theft. Likewise, if the risks of decentralized AI were proven to be fundamentally unmanageable through output-based verification, the case for universal access would weaken in favor of controlled, centralized distribution. We must evolve our legal frameworks to view data as the fuel for a new era of post-scarcity, rather than a commodity to be hoarded by the past. 🚀",
